1
00:00:02,336 --> 00:00:03,420
OKAY.

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:04,588
COME ON, AND
NO PEEKING.

3
00:00:04,588 --> 00:00:05,881
OUR EYES ARE CLOSED

4
00:00:05,881 --> 00:00:07,633
AND WE'RE ABOUT
TO CROSS THE STREET--

5
00:00:07,633 --> 00:00:09,551
VERY GOOD.

6
00:00:09,551 --> 00:00:11,428
OKAY... OPEN UP.

7
00:00:15,265 --> 00:00:16,976
WHAT DO YOU WANT
TO SHOW US?

8
00:00:16,976 --> 00:00:20,938
BECAUSE ALL I CAN SEE
IS THIS BITCHIN' VAN!

9
00:00:20,938 --> 00:00:22,982
YEAH. IT'S FOR OUR
CATERING BUSINESS.

10
00:00:22,982 --> 00:00:24,023
OH.

11
00:00:24,023 --> 00:00:26,193
OH, I THINK I KNOW THAT GIRL.

12
00:00:27,862 --> 00:00:29,446
Monica:
ALL RIGHT. UM...

13
00:00:29,446 --> 00:00:30,739
WE'RE NOT GOING TO REALLY
KEEP IT THIS WAY, THOUGH.

14
00:00:30,739 --> 00:00:31,991
NO?

15
00:00:31,991 --> 00:00:33,659
WE'RE GOING TO PAINT
OVER THE SWORD

16
00:00:33,659 --> 00:00:35,160
AND REPLACE IT
WITH A BAGUETTE.

17
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:36,996
OH.
MMM.

18
00:00:36,996 --> 00:00:39,331
UM, ALSO, WE DON'T KNOW
WHAT TO DO WITH THIS.

19
00:00:39,331 --> 00:00:40,290
( switch clicking )

20
00:00:42,376 --> 00:00:44,294
OH, YEAH.
I DEFINITELY KNOW HER.

21
00:00:51,468 --> 00:00:56,348
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

22
00:00:56,348 --> 00:00:58,893
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

23
00:00:58,893 --> 00:01:01,144
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

24
00:01:01,144 --> 00:01:06,149
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

25
00:01:06,149 --> 00:01:08,610
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN YOUR DAY ♪

26
00:01:08,610 --> 00:01:11,446
♪ YOUR WEEK, YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

27
00:01:11,446 --> 00:01:14,115
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

28
00:01:14,115 --> 00:01:16,326
♪ WHEN THE RAIN
STARTS TO POUR ♪

29
00:01:16,326 --> 00:01:19,120
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

30
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:21,498
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

31
00:01:21,498 --> 00:01:24,793
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

32
00:01:24,793 --> 00:01:29,757
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

33
00:01:35,804 --> 00:01:37,514
REMEMBER THAT GUY
FROM COOKING SCHOOL

34
00:01:37,514 --> 00:01:39,516
I TOLD YOU ABOUT THAT
PUT CILANTRO IN EVERYTHING?

35
00:01:39,516 --> 00:01:41,518
OH, SURE.
"CILANTRO" LARRY.

36
00:01:41,518 --> 00:01:44,103
YEAH. WELL, I'M GOING
TO FILL IN FOR HIM

37
00:01:44,103 --> 00:01:45,898
AS FOOD CRITIC
FOR THE CHELSEA REPORTER.

38
00:01:45,898 --> 00:01:49,234
WOW! MONICA,
WHAT AN AMAZING OPPORTUNITY

39
00:01:49,234 --> 00:01:52,487
TO INFLUENCE...
DOZENS OF PEOPLE.

40
00:01:55,032 --> 00:01:56,116
Phoebe:
HOW COULD YOU
HAVE SAID YES?

41
00:01:56,116 --> 00:01:57,451
WHAT ABOUT
OUR CATERING BUSINESS?

42
00:01:57,451 --> 00:01:59,369
OH, NO, NO.
IT'S JUST ONE NIGHT A WEEK.

43
00:01:59,369 --> 00:02:00,746
PLUS, I GET TO TAKE
ALL OF YOU OUT

44
00:02:00,746 --> 00:02:02,122
FOR A LOT OF
FREE DINNERS.

45
00:02:02,122 --> 00:02:03,540
HEY.
HEY.

46
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:05,084
OH, WELL, IN THAT CASE...

47
00:02:05,084 --> 00:02:07,002
HEY.

48
00:02:08,503 --> 00:02:10,089
THAT WAS ME HOPPING ON BOARD.

49
00:02:10,089 --> 00:02:11,214
OH.

50
00:02:11,214 --> 00:02:12,716
HEY, GUYS.

51
00:02:12,716 --> 00:02:15,761
HEY, ROSS,
QUICK QUESTION FOR YOU.

52
00:02:15,761 --> 00:02:19,138
ARE YOU READY TO PARTY?

53
00:02:19,138 --> 00:02:21,516
I DON'T KNOW. I COULD MAYBE
GO OUT FOR A COUPLE OF BEERS,

54
00:02:21,516 --> 00:02:24,436
BUT THERE'S THIS THING
ABOUT BUMBLEBEES

55
00:02:24,436 --> 00:02:27,147
ON THE DISCOVERY CHANNEL...

56
00:02:27,147 --> 00:02:28,774
NO, NO, NO.
I DON'T THINK YOU HEARD ME.

57
00:02:28,774 --> 00:02:31,401
ARE YOU READY... TO PARTY?

58
00:02:32,903 --> 00:02:34,404
NO!

59
00:02:34,404 --> 00:02:35,572
GANDALF?!

60
00:02:35,572 --> 00:02:36,949
GANDALF IS
COMING TO TOWN?

61
00:02:36,949 --> 00:02:38,241
KATHY'S WITH
HER PARENTS.

62
00:02:38,241 --> 00:02:39,576
I HAVE NOTHING TO DO.

63
00:02:39,576 --> 00:02:41,912
TOMORROW, WE ARE
PARTYING WITH GANDALF, DUDE!

64
00:02:41,912 --> 00:02:45,457
DUDE, WE ARE
SO GOING TO PARTY.

65
00:02:45,457 --> 00:02:46,792
YEAH!

66
00:02:46,792 --> 00:02:48,752
WOW! OKAY. DUDE ALERT.

67
00:02:50,629 --> 00:02:52,339
AND WHO IS THIS GUY?

68
00:02:52,339 --> 00:02:54,508
MIKE "GANDALF"
GANDERSON.

69
00:02:54,508 --> 00:02:57,136
ONLY, LIKE, THE FUNNEST
GUY IN THE WORLD.

70
00:02:57,136 --> 00:02:58,637
I'M GOING TO CALL
AND GET OFF WORK TOMORROW.

71
00:02:58,637 --> 00:03:00,555
I'M GOING TO CALL
AFTER YOU!

72
00:03:01,890 --> 00:03:03,684
THIS IS GOING
TO BE SO COOL, DUDE.

73
00:03:03,684 --> 00:03:05,019
WE NEVER PARTY ANYMORE.

74
00:03:05,019 --> 00:03:07,813
OOOOOOH!
OOOOOOH!

75
00:03:07,813 --> 00:03:10,482
WERE YOU GUYS SMOKING SOMETHING
IN THE BACK OF OUR VAN?

76
00:03:12,442 --> 00:03:14,611
REALLY. WHAT DO YOU MEAN,
WE NEVER HAVE FUN ANYMORE?

77
00:03:14,611 --> 00:03:16,030
YOU HAVE FUN WITH ME.

78
00:03:16,030 --> 00:03:17,405
REMEMBER THE TIME
WE SAW THOSE STRIPPERS

79
00:03:17,405 --> 00:03:22,077
AND YOU PAID ME 50 BUCKS
TO EAT THAT BOOK?

80
00:03:22,077 --> 00:03:23,620
JOEY, YOU
ARE GOING TO
LOVE THIS GUY.

81
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:26,081
GANDALF IS, LIKE,
THE PARTY WIZARD.

82
00:03:26,081 --> 00:03:28,291
WHY DO YOU
CALL HIM GANDALF?

83
00:03:28,291 --> 00:03:30,085
GANDALF THE WIZARD.

84
00:03:32,211 --> 00:03:34,006
HELLO. DIDN'T YOU READ
LORD OF THE RINGS

85
00:03:34,006 --> 00:03:34,965
IN HIGH SCHOOL?

86
00:03:36,215 --> 00:03:37,968
NO, I HAD SEX
IN HIGH SCHOOL.

87
00:03:43,473 --> 00:03:44,892
OH, UH... JOANNA?

88
00:03:44,892 --> 00:03:46,226
I WAS WONDERING

89
00:03:46,226 --> 00:03:48,812
IF I COULD
ASK YOU SOMETHING.

90
00:03:48,812 --> 00:03:50,814
THERE'S AN OPENING
FOR AN ASSISTANT BUYER

91
00:03:50,814 --> 00:03:52,024
IN JUNIOR MISS...

92
00:03:52,024 --> 00:03:53,859
THAT WOULD BE
A STEP DOWN FOR ME.

93
00:03:53,859 --> 00:03:56,486
NO, ACTUALLY,
I MEANT FOR ME.

94
00:03:56,486 --> 00:03:59,364
THE HIRING COMMITTEE IS
MEETING PEOPLE ALL DAY.

95
00:03:59,364 --> 00:04:01,241
OH. WELL,
I WISH I COULD SAY NO

96
00:04:01,241 --> 00:04:04,285
BUT I GUESS YOU CAN'T STAY
MY ASSISTANT FOREVER.

97
00:04:04,285 --> 00:04:06,371
NEITHER CAN YOU, SOPHIE,
BUT FOR DIFFERENT REASONS.

98
00:04:08,832 --> 00:04:11,001
I'M SO GLAD YOU DON'T
HAVE A PROBLEM WITH THIS

99
00:04:11,001 --> 00:04:13,378
OR I WOULDN'T HAVE
CONSIDERED APPLYING.

100
00:04:13,378 --> 00:04:15,130
REALLY? IN THAT CASE...

101
00:04:15,130 --> 00:04:17,465
THAT'S WHY I'M SO GLAD
THERE'S NO PROBLEM.

102
00:04:17,465 --> 00:04:19,885
IT'S FINE. ACTUALLY,
I'M ON THE HIRING COMMITTEE

103
00:04:19,885 --> 00:04:22,054
SO THERE'LL BE AT LEAST
ONE FRIENDLY FACE.

104
00:04:22,054 --> 00:04:23,388
OH, THAT'S GREAT.

105
00:04:23,388 --> 00:04:26,474
JUNIOR MISS
IS WHERE I STARTED.
REALLY?

106
00:04:26,474 --> 00:04:30,020
HAD TO SLEEP WITH
THE UGLIEST GUY
TO GET THAT JOB.

107
00:04:30,020 --> 00:04:31,354
OH... REALLY?

108
00:04:31,354 --> 00:04:34,274
NO!

109
00:04:34,274 --> 00:04:35,275
YEAH.

110
00:04:36,985 --> 00:04:39,947
I MEAN, NO, NO,
NO, NO, NO, NO.

111
00:04:39,947 --> 00:04:41,573
DON'T YOU WORRY. I'M SURE
WITH YOUR QUALIFICATIONS,

112
00:04:41,573 --> 00:04:44,659
YOU WON'T NEED TO SLEEP
WITH SOME GUY TO GET THE JOB.

113
00:04:44,659 --> 00:04:46,912
ALTHOUGH I MIGHT NEED
SOME CONVINCING.

114
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:49,581
WELL, UM...

115
00:04:49,581 --> 00:04:51,208
KIDDING!

116
00:04:51,208 --> 00:04:53,543
( both laughing )

117
00:04:53,543 --> 00:04:55,378
GOD, I FEEL WILD TODAY!

118
00:05:00,425 --> 00:05:02,427
OH, MAN,
I AM SO EXCITED

119
00:05:02,427 --> 00:05:04,554
I MAY VOMIT.

120
00:05:04,554 --> 00:05:06,431
WILL YOU CALM DOWN?

121
00:05:06,431 --> 00:05:08,892
HE'S JUST A HUMAN GUY.

122
00:05:08,892 --> 00:05:10,936
YOU DON'T UNDERSTAND.
GANDALF IS AMAZING.

123
00:05:10,936 --> 00:05:13,063
YOU NEVER KNOW
WHAT WILL END UP HAPPENING.

124
00:05:13,063 --> 00:05:14,940
YOU GO OUT FOR A COUPLE OF BEERS

125
00:05:14,940 --> 00:05:17,192
AND END UP ON A FISHING BOAT
TO NOVA SCOTIA.

126
00:05:17,192 --> 00:05:18,735
REALLY?

127
00:05:18,735 --> 00:05:20,946
OH, YEAH. IT'S BEAUTIFUL COUNTRY
UP THERE.

128
00:05:20,946 --> 00:05:24,449
HEY! OKAY, I GOT MY PASSPORT,

129
00:05:24,449 --> 00:05:25,951
FRESH SOCKS,

130
00:05:25,951 --> 00:05:28,411
AND A SNAKEBITE KIT.

131
00:05:28,411 --> 00:05:31,248
IT'S NOT GOING
TO BE EXACTLY LIKE LAST TIME.

132
00:05:32,958 --> 00:05:34,209
ALL RIGHT
I'LL SEE YOU GUYS.

133
00:05:34,209 --> 00:05:35,418
WHOA, WHOA.
WHOA, WHOA.

134
00:05:35,418 --> 00:05:37,129
WHOA, WHOA,
WHOA, WHOA, WHOA.

135
00:05:37,129 --> 00:05:39,338
I HAVE AN AUDITION.
I'LL HOOK UP WITH YOU LATER.

136
00:05:39,338 --> 00:05:41,049
WHERE WILL YOU BE
AROUND NOON?

137
00:05:41,049 --> 00:05:44,136
SOMEWHERE MAYBE
ALONG THE EQUATOR.

138
00:05:44,136 --> 00:05:45,720
( both laughing )

139
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:48,015
OKAY.

140
00:05:48,015 --> 00:05:49,933
( phone rings )

141
00:05:49,933 --> 00:05:51,268
HELLO.

142
00:05:51,268 --> 00:05:52,769
IT'S GANDALF!

143
00:05:52,769 --> 00:05:54,729
OOOOOOH!
OOOOOOH!

144
00:05:54,729 --> 00:05:56,857
SO, YOU IN TOWN?

145
00:05:59,567 --> 00:06:01,569
OH, WELL...

146
00:06:01,569 --> 00:06:03,362
WELL, MAYBE NEXT TIME THEN.

147
00:06:03,362 --> 00:06:06,325
WHAT HAPPENED?

148
00:06:06,325 --> 00:06:08,493
HE'S NOT GOING TO MAKE IT.
HE'S STUCK IN CHICAGO.

149
00:06:08,493 --> 00:06:10,078
OH, MAN!

150
00:06:10,078 --> 00:06:12,873
CHICAGO'S SO LUCKY.

151
00:06:12,873 --> 00:06:15,167
STUPID, USELESS

152
00:06:15,167 --> 00:06:17,127
CANADIAN MONEY!

153
00:06:22,966 --> 00:06:25,635
YOU HAVE A VERY
IMPRESSIVE RESUME, MS. GREEN.

154
00:06:25,635 --> 00:06:27,679
I ESPECIALLY LIKE
WHAT I SEE HERE

155
00:06:27,679 --> 00:06:30,098
ABOUT IMPLEMENTING
A NEW FILING SYSTEM.

156
00:06:30,098 --> 00:06:31,599
THANK YOU.

157
00:06:31,599 --> 00:06:33,310
FILING SYSTEM?

158
00:06:33,310 --> 00:06:34,728
YOU MEAN
THOSE LITTLE
COLORED LABELS

159
00:06:34,728 --> 00:06:36,395
YOU PUT ON
ALL THE FOLDERS?

160
00:06:36,395 --> 00:06:39,024
IT BRIGHTENED UP THE INSIDE
OF THE FILING CABINETS.

161
00:06:39,024 --> 00:06:41,735
WELL, THEY, UH... THEY...

162
00:06:41,735 --> 00:06:44,529
THEY DID MORE THAN THAT.

163
00:06:44,529 --> 00:06:46,365
I NOTICE THAT
YOU'VE BEEN ENTRUSTED

164
00:06:46,365 --> 00:06:49,450
WITH A LOT OF RATHER
IMPORTANT RESPONSIBILITIES.

165
00:06:49,450 --> 00:06:54,164
YES. JOANNA REALLY HAS BEEN
AN INCREDIBLE MENTOR TO ME.

166
00:06:54,164 --> 00:06:55,623
RACHEL HAS
BEEN INCREDIBLE

167
00:06:55,623 --> 00:06:57,792
AT GETTING
MY MORNING
BAGEL FOR ME.

168
00:06:57,792 --> 00:07:00,212
IT'S AMAZING HOW
SHE GETS IT RIGHT
ALMOST EVERY TIME.

169
00:07:00,212 --> 00:07:01,713
I... I... OF COURSE...

170
00:07:01,713 --> 00:07:04,632
I HAVE MORE RESPONSIBILITIES
THAN THAT.

171
00:07:04,632 --> 00:07:06,718
OF COURSE.
WELL, THERE'S
THE COFFEE, TOO.

172
00:07:06,718 --> 00:07:10,430
RACHEL CAN CARRY
TWO THINGS AT ONCE.

173
00:07:10,430 --> 00:07:12,391
THAT'S... THAT'S VERY GOOD.

174
00:07:12,391 --> 00:07:13,892
NOW...

175
00:07:13,892 --> 00:07:15,936
A, UH...

176
00:07:15,936 --> 00:07:17,436
BIG PART OF THIS JOB

177
00:07:17,436 --> 00:07:19,064
IS CULTIVATING
PERSONAL RELATIONSHIPS,

178
00:07:19,064 --> 00:07:21,233
ESPECIALLY WITH DESIGNERS.

179
00:07:21,233 --> 00:07:23,902
YES, I REALIZE THAT.
RACHEL SHOULDN'T
HAVE ANY PROBLEM.

180
00:07:23,902 --> 00:07:25,445
HER ONLY PROBLEM
MIGHT BE GETTING

181
00:07:25,445 --> 00:07:28,531
TOO FRIENDLY, IF
YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN?

182
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:30,658
I LOVE WORKING WITH DESIGNERS.

183
00:07:30,658 --> 00:07:32,244
WITH THEM, UNDER THEM.

184
00:07:32,244 --> 00:07:34,704
WHAT'S THE
DIFFERENCE,
HEY, RACH?

185
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:41,836
HEY, MY FIRST REVIEW IS OUT.

186
00:07:41,836 --> 00:07:44,714
OH! OH,
THE CHELSEA REPORTER.

187
00:07:44,714 --> 00:07:48,135
OH, THESE USED
TO KEEP ME SO WARM.

188
00:07:48,135 --> 00:07:50,469
RIGHT. LOOK,
I'M ON THE BACK PAGE.

189
00:07:50,469 --> 00:07:51,805
OH! OKAY.

190
00:07:51,805 --> 00:07:53,681
"WOULD I GO BACK
TO ALESSANDRO'S?

191
00:07:53,681 --> 00:07:55,976
"SURE. BUT I'D HAVE
TO ORDER TWO MEALS--

192
00:07:55,976 --> 00:07:57,185
"ONE FOR ME
AND ONE FOR THE GUY

193
00:07:57,185 --> 00:07:59,438
POINTING THE GUN
TO MY HEAD."

194
00:07:59,438 --> 00:08:02,523
WOW! YOU REALLY
LAID INTO THIS PLACE.

195
00:08:02,523 --> 00:08:05,484
THEY DON'T PAY ME
A PENNY A WORD TO MAKE FRIENDS.

196
00:08:05,484 --> 00:08:07,570
I GOT TO GO.
I FOUND A GUY

197
00:08:07,570 --> 00:08:09,323
WHO CAN FIX UP
THE VAN FOR CATERING.

198
00:08:09,323 --> 00:08:10,531
OH, DO YOU WANT ME TO GO
WITH YOU?

199
00:08:10,531 --> 00:08:12,159
NO, NO, IT'S OKAY.

200
00:08:12,159 --> 00:08:13,910
BUT ARE WE SURE
WE DON'T WANT THE WATERBED?

201
00:08:15,412 --> 00:08:17,080
HAVEN'T WE MADE THIS DECISION?

202
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:18,457
YEAH. ALL RIGHT.

203
00:08:19,958 --> 00:08:21,709
BYE.
BYE.

204
00:08:23,837 --> 00:08:25,797
( intercom buzzes )

205
00:08:27,632 --> 00:08:29,134
WHO IS IT?

206
00:08:29,134 --> 00:08:31,261
It's Alessandro,
from Alessandro's.

207
00:08:32,887 --> 00:08:34,306
OH, MY GOD.

208
00:08:34,306 --> 00:08:35,890
I want to talk to you
about your review.

209
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:38,310
OH, MY GOD. OH, MY GOD.

210
00:08:38,310 --> 00:08:40,645
CALL ME ON THE PHONE.

211
00:08:40,645 --> 00:08:42,689
What, so you can hang up on me?

212
00:08:42,689 --> 00:08:44,941
LOOK. I'M NEVER GOING
TO LET YOU UP

213
00:08:44,941 --> 00:08:46,776
SO YOU MAY AS WELL JUST GO AWAY.

214
00:08:46,776 --> 00:08:48,111
Give me a chance to...

215
00:08:48,111 --> 00:08:50,280
Phoebe:
You need to get in? Here you go.

216
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:51,531
NO, PHOEBE!

217
00:08:51,531 --> 00:08:52,991
Oh, hey, Monica.

218
00:08:58,705 --> 00:08:59,956
I WANT A RETRACTION.

219
00:08:59,956 --> 00:09:02,334
OUR FOOD IS NOT
INEDIBLE SWILL!

220
00:09:02,334 --> 00:09:04,002
I COULDN'T EAT IT.

221
00:09:04,002 --> 00:09:05,545
I HAVE FIVE FRIENDS
WHO COULDN'T EAT IT

222
00:09:05,545 --> 00:09:08,673
AND ONE OF THEM EATS BOOKS.

223
00:09:08,673 --> 00:09:11,259
WELL, OUR SERVICE IS
NOT GROSSLY INCOMPETENT.

224
00:09:11,259 --> 00:09:14,304
THE WAITER CARRIED
THE BREADSTICKS IN HIS PANTS.

225
00:09:15,889 --> 00:09:19,518
WELL... YOU SAID THAT
WE ACCEPT THE DISCOVER CARD

226
00:09:19,518 --> 00:09:22,187
WHICH WE DO NOT.

227
00:09:22,187 --> 00:09:26,024
ALL RIGHT. THAT I'LL RETRACT,
BUT I STAND BY MY REVIEW.

228
00:09:26,024 --> 00:09:28,443
I KNOW FOOD, AND THAT WASN'T IT.

229
00:09:28,443 --> 00:09:31,029
YOUR MARINARA SAUCE
TASTES LIKE TOMATO JUICE.

230
00:09:31,029 --> 00:09:33,073
YOU SHOULD SERVE IT WITH VODKA
AND A PIECE OF CELERY.

231
00:09:34,657 --> 00:09:36,617
I'M PROUD OF THAT SAUCE.
IT'S DELICIOUS.

232
00:09:36,617 --> 00:09:38,453
OH, MY GOD!

233
00:09:38,453 --> 00:09:41,081
YOU OWN AN ITALIAN RESTAURANT
AND YOU THINK THAT TASTES GOOD?

234
00:09:41,081 --> 00:09:42,374
WHERE ARE YOU EVEN FROM?

235
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:46,503
LEBANON.

236
00:09:46,503 --> 00:09:48,380
HAND ME THOSE TOMATOES.

237
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:50,257
I'M GOING TO SHOW YOU
WHAT IT SHOULD TASTE LIKE.

238
00:09:50,257 --> 00:09:53,051
COME ON.
HAND THEM TO ME.

239
00:09:53,051 --> 00:09:54,344
HOW LONG IS THIS GOING
TO TAKE, BECAUSE I GOT

240
00:09:54,344 --> 00:09:57,556
ANOTHER CRITIC
I GOT TO GO YELL AT.

241
00:10:02,227 --> 00:10:04,020
( clears throat ):
UH, JOANNA?

242
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:06,022
I WANT TO TALK
ABOUT THAT INTERVIEW.

243
00:10:06,022 --> 00:10:08,483
I THOUGHT IT WENT VERY WELL.

244
00:10:08,483 --> 00:10:10,777
NO, IT DIDN'T.

245
00:10:10,777 --> 00:10:13,238
THAT'S WHAT I WANT
TO TALK TO YOU ABOUT.

246
00:10:14,573 --> 00:10:16,324
NOW, JUST TO BRIEF YOU...

247
00:10:18,743 --> 00:10:20,495
I MAY CRY

248
00:10:20,495 --> 00:10:23,873
BUT THEY ARE NOT
TEARS OF SADNESS

249
00:10:23,873 --> 00:10:25,917
OR OF ANGER

250
00:10:25,917 --> 00:10:28,545
BUT JUST OF ME HAVING
THIS DISCUSSION WITH YOU.

251
00:10:28,545 --> 00:10:31,381
RACHEL, PLEASE.
DON'T MAKE A SCENE.

252
00:10:31,381 --> 00:10:34,175
THERE'S NOBODY HERE.

253
00:10:34,175 --> 00:10:35,260
SOPHIE, GET IN HERE!

254
00:10:37,554 --> 00:10:40,223
YOU SEE? YOU'RE MAKING
SOPHIE UNCOMFORTABLE.

255
00:10:40,223 --> 00:10:42,976
SHE'S NOT MAKING ME
UNCOMFORTABLE.

256
00:10:42,976 --> 00:10:45,353
CONGRATULATIONS. YOU CROSSED THE
LINE INTO COMPLETELY USELESS.

257
00:10:45,353 --> 00:10:46,396
GET OUT.

258
00:10:48,898 --> 00:10:51,067
DO YOU WANT ME TO QUIT?

259
00:10:51,067 --> 00:10:52,193
WHAT?

260
00:10:52,193 --> 00:10:53,987
WHAT WOULD MAKE YOU THINK THAT?

261
00:10:53,987 --> 00:10:57,073
WELL, ALL OF THOSE THINGS
THAT YOU SAID IN THE INTERVIEW.

262
00:10:57,073 --> 00:10:58,658
IF YOU BELIEVE ANY OF THEM

263
00:10:58,658 --> 00:11:00,577
I MUST NOT BE
A VERY GOOD ASSISTANT.

264
00:11:02,537 --> 00:11:03,913
YOU KNOW WHAT?

265
00:11:03,913 --> 00:11:07,708
I AM JUST GOING
TO PACK UP MY DESK...

266
00:11:07,708 --> 00:11:09,127
( rattling drawer )

267
00:11:09,127 --> 00:11:11,712
AND I WILL BE GONE
BY THE END OF THE DAY.

268
00:11:16,092 --> 00:11:17,594
WELL, I GUESS
THERE'S NO USE

269
00:11:17,594 --> 00:11:19,137
ME STICKING AROUND
TILL THE END OF THE DAY.

270
00:11:19,137 --> 00:11:21,431
ALL RIGHT.
WAIT, WAIT, WAIT, WAIT.

271
00:11:21,431 --> 00:11:23,433
YOU CAN PUT
YOUR SAD, LITTLE MUFFIN

272
00:11:23,433 --> 00:11:24,976
BACK IN ITS DRAWER.

273
00:11:24,976 --> 00:11:27,270
IF YOU MUST KNOW
THE TRUTH,

274
00:11:27,270 --> 00:11:30,357
I DIDN'T WANT TO LOSE
A PERFECTLY GOOD ASSISTANT.

275
00:11:30,357 --> 00:11:31,774
WHAT?

276
00:11:31,774 --> 00:11:33,943
THAT'S WHY I SAID
ALL THOSE THINGS

277
00:11:33,943 --> 00:11:36,613
ABOUT YOUR FLIRTING
AND YOUR DRINKING.

278
00:11:36,613 --> 00:11:38,448
MY DRINKING?

279
00:11:38,448 --> 00:11:41,284
OH. I MUST HAVE SAID THAT
AFTER YOU LEFT.

280
00:11:43,161 --> 00:11:45,163
SAID WHAT, EXACTLY?

281
00:11:45,163 --> 00:11:47,832
YOU ENJOY THE OCCASIONAL
DRINK...ING BINGE.

282
00:11:47,832 --> 00:11:49,876
( gasps )

283
00:11:49,876 --> 00:11:51,085
OH, MY GOD!

284
00:11:51,085 --> 00:11:53,171
OH! THAT IS IT!
I AM LEAVING!

285
00:11:53,171 --> 00:11:55,048
YOU ARE JUST
A HORRIBLE PERSON.

286
00:11:55,048 --> 00:11:56,841
NO, WAIT, WAIT,
WAIT, WAIT, WAIT.

287
00:11:56,841 --> 00:11:59,469
IF YOU'RE GOING TO GET
ALL SENSITIVE ABOUT IT.

288
00:11:59,469 --> 00:12:01,137
I DON'T WANT
TO LOSE YOU.

289
00:12:01,137 --> 00:12:03,682
WHAT IF I CREATE
A POSITION FOR YOU?

290
00:12:03,682 --> 00:12:07,018
I'LL MAKE YOU ASSISTANT BUYER
IN THIS DEPARTMENT.

291
00:12:07,018 --> 00:12:09,604
SAY MORE THINGS
LIKE THAT.

292
00:12:09,604 --> 00:12:11,565
UM...

293
00:12:11,565 --> 00:12:13,066
YOU CAN HAVE
YOUR OWN OFFICE

294
00:12:13,066 --> 00:12:14,775
AND A RAISE,
EFFECTIVE TOMORROW.

295
00:12:14,775 --> 00:12:16,528
I'D NEED
AN EXPENSE ACCOUNT.

296
00:12:16,528 --> 00:12:18,071
DONE.

297
00:12:18,071 --> 00:12:19,239
AND AN ASSISTANT.

298
00:12:19,239 --> 00:12:21,199
SOPHIE, GET IN HERE.

299
00:12:23,034 --> 00:12:25,495
However, it seems
like a lifetime, doesn't it?

300
00:12:25,495 --> 00:12:27,914
Starting when Stefano
used Kristin...

301
00:12:27,914 --> 00:12:30,124
HEY. WHAT ARE
YOU GUYS DOING HERE?

302
00:12:30,124 --> 00:12:33,044
I THOUGHT YOU'D BE OUT
PARTYING WITH GAN...DORF.

303
00:12:33,044 --> 00:12:34,753
IT'S GANDALF

304
00:12:34,753 --> 00:12:36,881
AND HE'S NOT COMING.

305
00:12:36,881 --> 00:12:38,966
SO YOU BEEN SITTING
AROUND ALL MORNING?

306
00:12:38,966 --> 00:12:40,385
NO.

307
00:12:40,385 --> 00:12:43,054
I BALANCED
MY CHECKBOOK.

308
00:12:43,054 --> 00:12:45,056
YEAH, AND I GAVE
FIRST NAMES

309
00:12:45,056 --> 00:12:46,849
TO ALL
THE FOOSBALL PLAYERS.

310
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:51,229
I CAN'T BELIEVE HE DIDN'T COME.

311
00:12:51,229 --> 00:12:52,731
SO WHAT IF HE DIDN'T COME?

312
00:12:52,731 --> 00:12:54,691
WE CAN GO OUT
AND PARTY OURSELVES.

313
00:12:54,691 --> 00:12:55,983
OH, NO.
YOU KNOW,

314
00:12:55,983 --> 00:12:58,528
WITH GANDALF,
WE'D BE OUT ALL NIGHT.

315
00:12:58,528 --> 00:13:00,196
YEAH. WE'D MEET... WE'D MEET

316
00:13:00,196 --> 00:13:02,990
TOTAL STRANGERS
AND HANG OUT WITH THEM.

317
00:13:02,990 --> 00:13:05,784
WELL, WE COULD DO THAT.

318
00:13:05,784 --> 00:13:09,038
( sadly ):
THERE WAS OTHER
STUFF, TOO.

319
00:13:09,038 --> 00:13:10,998
WE'LL DO IT
ALL, AND BETTER.

320
00:13:10,998 --> 00:13:13,084
LOOK, AFTER TONIGHT
GANDALF WILL WANT

321
00:13:13,084 --> 00:13:15,169
TO PARTY WITH US, DUDE.
COME ON!

322
00:13:15,169 --> 00:13:18,131
YEAH!
YEAH!

323
00:13:18,131 --> 00:13:19,633
YEAH! IT'S NOT LIKE
WE DON'T KNOW HOW TO PARTY.

324
00:13:19,633 --> 00:13:21,718
YEAH! ALL RIGHT!
LET'S GO!

325
00:13:21,718 --> 00:13:23,844
MAYBE WE COULD END UP
ON A BOAT AGAIN?

326
00:13:23,844 --> 00:13:24,845
YEAH!
YEAH!

327
00:13:24,845 --> 00:13:25,846
WELL, ALL RIGHT!

328
00:13:25,846 --> 00:13:27,056
YEAH!

329
00:13:27,056 --> 00:13:28,224
HEY, HEY, HEY.

330
00:13:28,224 --> 00:13:30,393
WHEN, UH...
WHEN WERE WE ON A BOAT?

331
00:13:30,393 --> 00:13:32,270
REMEMBER
THAT REALLY COLD MORNING

332
00:13:32,270 --> 00:13:34,981
WHEN YOU WOKE UP AND THOSE DOGS
WERE LICKING YOUR FACE?

333
00:13:34,981 --> 00:13:36,983
YEAH.
THOSE WERE SEALS, MAN.

334
00:13:44,031 --> 00:13:46,284
HEY, LITTLE
QUESTION FOR YOU,

335
00:13:46,284 --> 00:13:48,202
HOW DO YOU THINK
THIS SUIT WOULD LOOK
ON AN ASSISTANT...?

336
00:13:48,202 --> 00:13:50,204
THE OWNER OF ALESSANDRO'S
CAME OVER TO YELL AT ME

337
00:13:50,204 --> 00:13:52,957
BUT I MADE HIM SOME SAUCE,
AND HE OFFERED ME THE JOB
AS HEAD CHEF.

338
00:13:52,957 --> 00:13:55,918
OH, MY GOD! YOU JUST RUINED
THE THING IS WAS PRACTICING

339
00:13:55,918 --> 00:13:57,796
THE WHOLE WAY HOME
BUT I'M SO HAPPY!

340
00:13:59,172 --> 00:14:00,548
I KNOW! CAN YOU BELIEVE IT?

341
00:14:00,548 --> 00:14:02,592
I FINALLY
GET TO RUN MY OWN KITCHEN.

342
00:14:02,592 --> 00:14:05,428
OH, YOU'VE WAITED SO LONG.
AW...

343
00:14:05,428 --> 00:14:06,763
HEY.

344
00:14:06,763 --> 00:14:08,765
HEY, PHEEBS,
QUICK QUESTION FOR YOU:

345
00:14:08,765 --> 00:14:10,600
HOW DO YOU THINK
THIS SUIT WOULD LOOK

346
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:13,019
ON AN ASSISTANT BUYER
AT BLOOMINGDALE'S?

347
00:14:13,019 --> 00:14:14,437
I DON'T KNOW.

348
00:14:14,437 --> 00:14:17,524
IT WOULD TOTALLY DEPEND
ON HER COLORING, AND...

349
00:14:17,524 --> 00:14:19,192
YOU GOT THE JOB!

350
00:14:19,192 --> 00:14:20,943
YOU GOT THE JOB?!

351
00:14:20,943 --> 00:14:22,195
WHY DIDN'T YOU TELL ME?

352
00:14:24,739 --> 00:14:26,616
OH, IT'S
GOING TO BE SO GREAT!

353
00:14:26,616 --> 00:14:28,576
I'M GOING TO GET
TO HELP DECIDE WHAT WE SELL

354
00:14:28,576 --> 00:14:31,412
AND I'M GOING TO HAVE AN OFFICE
WITH WALLS AND EVERYTHING.

355
00:14:31,412 --> 00:14:34,541
I'M GOING TO HAVE WALLS!

356
00:14:34,541 --> 00:14:36,917
OKAY. IS THIS
THE DAY OF GOOD NEWS OR WHAT?

357
00:14:36,917 --> 00:14:39,295
I GOT US A JOB--
THE WEDDING RECEPTION.

358
00:14:39,295 --> 00:14:40,380
( chuckles )

359
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:41,881
OH! UM...

360
00:14:41,881 --> 00:14:44,467
PHOEBE, I KIND OF NEED
TO TALK TO YOU ABOUT THAT.

361
00:14:44,467 --> 00:14:45,760
( clears throat )

362
00:14:47,512 --> 00:14:50,515
UM... WELL, I-I-I THINK
IT MIGHT BE TIME FOR ME

363
00:14:50,515 --> 00:14:53,976
TO TAKE A STEP BACK
FROM THE CATERING.

364
00:14:53,976 --> 00:14:57,063
BUT WE'VE ONLY HAD ONE JOB.

365
00:14:57,063 --> 00:14:59,106
I KNOW, BUT NOW
WE HAVE THIS SECOND ONE

366
00:14:59,106 --> 00:15:02,694
AND IT JUST... IT FEELS LIKE
IT'S SNOWBALLING, YOU KNOW?

367
00:15:02,694 --> 00:15:04,445
YEAH. WHAT ARE YOU SAYING?

368
00:15:04,445 --> 00:15:07,741
I GOT OFFERED THE HEAD CHEF JOB
AT ALESSANDRO'S.

369
00:15:07,741 --> 00:15:09,033
WHAT?

370
00:15:09,033 --> 00:15:10,993
IT'S OKAY.
IF YOU THINK ABOUT IT

371
00:15:10,993 --> 00:15:12,662
YOU DON'T REALLY NEED ME
FOR THE BUSINESS.

372
00:15:12,662 --> 00:15:16,082
YOU'RE THE COOK!

373
00:15:16,082 --> 00:15:18,793
WITHOUT YOU, IT'S JUST ME
DRIVING UP TO PEOPLE'S HOUSES

374
00:15:18,793 --> 00:15:20,754
WITH EMPTY TRAYS
AND ASKING FOR MONEY.

375
00:15:24,424 --> 00:15:26,843
ALL RIGHT, BUT, UM...

376
00:15:26,843 --> 00:15:29,178
WELL, I'LL-I'LL PAY YOU BACK
ALL THE MONEY YOU INVESTED

377
00:15:29,178 --> 00:15:31,055
AND YOU CAN KEEP THE VAN.

378
00:15:31,055 --> 00:15:32,515
FOR WHAT?

379
00:15:34,058 --> 00:15:35,852
I CAN'T BELIEVE THIS.

380
00:15:35,852 --> 00:15:37,353
I GOT TO GET OUT
OF HERE.

381
00:15:37,353 --> 00:15:38,938
OH, PHOEBE, WAIT A MINUTE.

382
00:15:43,192 --> 00:15:44,819
I'M AN ASSISTANT BUYER!

383
00:15:49,949 --> 00:15:51,576
WE'LL GET A LITTLE COFFEE

384
00:15:51,576 --> 00:15:53,578
GET ENERGIZED,
AND WE'LL HEAD BACK OUT.

385
00:15:53,578 --> 00:15:54,579
YEAH. ALL RIGHT.

386
00:15:54,579 --> 00:15:55,538
OKAY.

387
00:15:59,041 --> 00:16:01,085
SO, WE'RE
HAVING FUN, RIGHT?

388
00:16:01,085 --> 00:16:03,045
WE DON'T NEED THAT WIZARD GUY.

389
00:16:03,045 --> 00:16:05,799
WE HIT A COUPLE OF CLUBS,
TALKED TO SOME STRANGERS

390
00:16:05,799 --> 00:16:07,508
AND AFTER THIS

391
00:16:07,508 --> 00:16:10,136
WE'LL GO DOWN TO THE DOCKS
AND SEE ABOUT THAT BOAT THING.

392
00:16:11,930 --> 00:16:14,682
I'M KIND OF BEAT.

393
00:16:14,682 --> 00:16:18,018
ACTUALLY...
ME, TOO.

394
00:16:18,018 --> 00:16:19,312
ARE YOU SERIOUS?

395
00:16:19,312 --> 00:16:20,521
YEAH.
YEAH.

396
00:16:20,521 --> 00:16:22,440
THANK GOD. I'M EXHAUSTED.

397
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:24,609
( sighing )

398
00:16:24,609 --> 00:16:26,110
SO, YOU GUYS
WANT COFFEES?

399
00:16:26,110 --> 00:16:28,279
YEAH, BUT I DON'T WANT
TO BE UP TOO LATE

400
00:16:28,279 --> 00:16:29,530
SO I'LL HAVE A DECAF.

401
00:16:29,530 --> 00:16:31,324
YEAH. ME, TOO.

402
00:16:31,324 --> 00:16:32,951
ACTUALLY, COULD I GET
SOME HOT WATER

403
00:16:32,951 --> 00:16:35,369
WITH A LITTLE LEMON?

404
00:16:35,369 --> 00:16:38,706
I THINK I STRAINED MY VOICE
SCREAMING IN THERE.

405
00:16:38,706 --> 00:16:40,959
DOES IT HAVE TO BE
SO LOUD?

406
00:16:40,959 --> 00:16:43,002
OH, I CAN'T HEAR
A WORD YOU'RE SAYING

407
00:16:43,002 --> 00:16:44,462
MY EARS
ARE RINGING SO BAD.

408
00:16:44,462 --> 00:16:45,797
I'M JUST GLAD
I BROUGHT

409
00:16:45,797 --> 00:16:47,757
THAT EXTRA PAIR
OF SOCKS, YOU KNOW?

410
00:16:47,757 --> 00:16:49,216
I USED THEM AS MITTENS.

411
00:16:49,216 --> 00:16:50,468
I DIDN'T
WANT TO TOUCH A THING

412
00:16:50,468 --> 00:16:52,136
IN THAT LAST PLACE.

413
00:16:56,474 --> 00:16:58,768
HOW SAD ARE WE?

414
00:16:58,768 --> 00:17:00,520
YEAH. I KNOW.

415
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:02,229
YOU KNOW WHAT? WE'RE NOT SAD.

416
00:17:02,229 --> 00:17:03,690
WE'RE NOT SAD.

417
00:17:03,690 --> 00:17:05,608
WE'RE JUST NOT 21 ANYMORE,
YOU KNOW?

418
00:17:05,608 --> 00:17:07,151
I'M 29 YEARS OLD, DAMN IT

419
00:17:07,151 --> 00:17:09,028
AND I WANT TO SIT
IN A COMFORTABLE CHAIR

420
00:17:09,028 --> 00:17:10,404
AND WATCH TELEVISION

421
00:17:10,404 --> 00:17:12,365
AND GO TO SLEEP
AT A REASONABLE HOUR.

422
00:17:12,365 --> 00:17:13,366
YEAH.
YEAH.

423
00:17:13,366 --> 00:17:14,367
YEAH, AND I LIKE

424
00:17:14,367 --> 00:17:15,952
TO HANG OUT
IN A QUIET PLACE

425
00:17:15,952 --> 00:17:17,537
WHERE I CAN TALK
TO MY FRIENDS.

426
00:17:17,537 --> 00:17:18,788
YEAH.
YEAH.

427
00:17:18,788 --> 00:17:20,665
AND SO WHAT
IF I LIKE TO GO HOME

428
00:17:20,665 --> 00:17:22,542
THROW ON SOME KENNY G
AND TAKE A BATH?

429
00:17:26,671 --> 00:17:28,965
WE'RE 29, WE'RE NOT WOMEN.

430
00:17:36,723 --> 00:17:38,808
OH, THERE YOU ARE.

431
00:17:40,100 --> 00:17:41,352
OKAY. I'M-I'M GLAD

432
00:17:41,352 --> 00:17:43,187
THAT YOU DECIDED
TO HEAR ME OUT.

433
00:17:43,187 --> 00:17:45,105
OKAY. I'M HEARING.

434
00:17:45,105 --> 00:17:48,275
OKAY. I'VE BEEN
DOING A LOT OF
THINKING-- A LOT--

435
00:17:48,275 --> 00:17:51,529
AND, WELL, I CAME UP WITH
A WHOLE BUNCH OF BUSINESSES

436
00:17:51,529 --> 00:17:53,364
THAT YOU CAN DO
WITH YOUR VAN.

437
00:17:53,364 --> 00:17:57,618
OKAY. UM... YOU COULD BE
A FLOWER DELIVERY PERSON.

438
00:17:57,618 --> 00:17:58,703
WHAT?

439
00:17:58,703 --> 00:17:59,704
OR...

440
00:17:59,704 --> 00:18:01,205
A BAKERY DELIVERY PERSON?

441
00:18:01,205 --> 00:18:02,289
( stammering )

442
00:18:02,289 --> 00:18:03,583
PIZZA?

443
00:18:03,583 --> 00:18:06,210
MONICA!

444
00:18:06,210 --> 00:18:09,380
ALL RIGHT. I'VE GOT A WHOLE
BUNCH OF STUFF IN THIS AREA

445
00:18:09,380 --> 00:18:10,757
BUT I'M GETTING
THE FEELING

446
00:18:10,757 --> 00:18:13,009
THAT YOU DON'T
WANT TO DELIVER.

447
00:18:13,009 --> 00:18:14,385
NO.

448
00:18:14,385 --> 00:18:15,344
OKAY.

449
00:18:17,388 --> 00:18:19,974
AND I'M GUESSING IF YOU
DON'T WANT TO DELIVER

450
00:18:19,974 --> 00:18:22,810
YOU PROBABLY DON'T WANT
TO PICK UP STUFF, EITHER.

451
00:18:22,810 --> 00:18:24,687
NO.

452
00:18:29,316 --> 00:18:31,277
YOU KNOW WHAT?

453
00:18:31,277 --> 00:18:33,071
LET'S DO THE CATERING BUSINESS.

454
00:18:33,071 --> 00:18:34,572
REALLY? ARE YOU SURE?

455
00:18:34,572 --> 00:18:36,449
YEAH. YOU KNOW, I-I...

456
00:18:36,449 --> 00:18:38,576
I MADE A COMMITMENT
TO YOU, AND...

457
00:18:38,576 --> 00:18:40,160
YOU KNOW, IT'D-IT'D BE FUN.

458
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:41,746
OH, IT WILL BE FUN!

459
00:18:41,746 --> 00:18:43,873
OH, YAY!

460
00:18:43,873 --> 00:18:46,166
OKAY. LET'S PLAN
THE WEDDING RECEPTION.

461
00:18:46,166 --> 00:18:47,167
OKAY.

462
00:18:47,167 --> 00:18:48,544
( giggles )

463
00:18:50,964 --> 00:18:51,923
WOW.

464
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:54,968
YOU REALLY WANTED ME

465
00:18:54,968 --> 00:18:56,636
TO DO SOMETHING
WITH THIS VAN.

466
00:19:01,265 --> 00:19:02,349
YOU KNOW WHAT?

467
00:19:02,349 --> 00:19:04,268
I WANT YOU
TO TAKE THE CHEF JOB.

468
00:19:04,268 --> 00:19:05,812
REALLY?

469
00:19:05,812 --> 00:19:07,271
YEAH.

470
00:19:07,271 --> 00:19:09,148
THAT'S WHAT
YOU REALLY WANT.

471
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:11,776
YEAH. I DON'T WANT TO BE
THE REASON YOU'RE UNHAPPY.

472
00:19:11,776 --> 00:19:13,611
THAT WOULD JUST
MAKE ME UNHAPPY

473
00:19:13,611 --> 00:19:17,364
AND I REALLY DON'T WANT TO BE
THE REASON I'M UNHAPPY.

474
00:19:17,364 --> 00:19:18,324
THANK YOU.

475
00:19:21,702 --> 00:19:22,954
BESIDES, IT MIGHT
BE KIND OF FUN

476
00:19:22,954 --> 00:19:24,246
TO FORM THE NEW A-TEAM.

477
00:19:34,048 --> 00:19:35,591
Rachel:
OH, HI, MRS. LYNCH.

478
00:19:35,591 --> 00:19:37,301
IS JOANNA IN ALREADY?

479
00:19:37,301 --> 00:19:40,220
OH, MY GOODNESS.
YOU HAVEN'T HEARD.

480
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:41,514
HEARD WHAT?

481
00:19:41,514 --> 00:19:45,184
JOANNA...
PASSED AWAY LAST NIGHT.

482
00:19:45,184 --> 00:19:48,062
OH, MY GOD! HOW?

483
00:19:48,062 --> 00:19:51,107
WELL, SHE WAS LEAVING WORK,
AND SHE WAS HIT BY A CAB.

484
00:19:51,107 --> 00:19:52,441
OH, MY GOD!

485
00:19:52,441 --> 00:19:53,943
OH, I CANNOT BELIEVE IT.

486
00:19:53,943 --> 00:19:55,778
OH, I KNOW.

487
00:19:55,778 --> 00:19:58,865
OH, GOD. OH, GOD...

488
00:20:00,783 --> 00:20:03,327
OH, GOD.

489
00:20:03,327 --> 00:20:06,246
I DIDN'T REALIZE
THAT YOU WERE SO CLOSE.

490
00:20:06,246 --> 00:20:08,958
YES... SO CLOSE.

491
00:20:11,502 --> 00:20:14,296
MRS. LYNCH, I KNOW THAT
THIS IS AN EMOTIONAL

492
00:20:14,296 --> 00:20:17,800
AND DIFFICULT TIME
FOR ALL OF US...

493
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:21,554
BUT BY ANY CHANCE DID JOANNA
SEND ANY PAPERWORK YOUR WAY

494
00:20:21,554 --> 00:20:24,849
BEFORE... IT HAPPENED?

495
00:20:24,849 --> 00:20:27,185
NO, NOTHING.

496
00:20:27,185 --> 00:20:28,435
IMAGINE...

497
00:20:28,435 --> 00:20:30,813
IF SHE'D JUST
STEPPED OFF THAT CURB

498
00:20:30,813 --> 00:20:31,939
A FEW SECONDS LATER.

499
00:20:31,939 --> 00:20:33,941
OH, YES, YES.

500
00:20:33,941 --> 00:20:37,319
JUST A FEW SECONDS AND
SHE'D STILL BE WITH US.

501
00:20:37,319 --> 00:20:40,073
NOTHING ABOUT AN
ASSISTANT BUYER OR...?

502
00:20:40,073 --> 00:20:41,281
I'M SORRY.

503
00:20:41,281 --> 00:20:42,783
I HAVE TO GO.

504
00:20:42,783 --> 00:20:44,744
( weeping )

505
00:20:44,744 --> 00:20:46,328
( cheerfully ):
GOOD MORNING.

506
00:20:46,328 --> 00:20:47,538
OH, SOPHIE, I GUESS

507
00:20:47,538 --> 00:20:49,373
YOU DIDN'T HEAR ABOUT JOANNA.

508
00:20:49,373 --> 00:20:51,000
I SURE DID.

509
00:20:57,548 --> 00:20:59,008
I'M SO EXCITED

510
00:20:59,008 --> 00:21:00,551
ABOUT HAVING MONICA
COME ON BOARD WITH US

511
00:21:00,551 --> 00:21:04,346
ALTHOUGH I DO FEEL BAD
ABOUT HAVING FIRED CHEF EMILIO.

512
00:21:04,346 --> 00:21:06,682
IT IS LIKE LOSING
A MEMBER OF THE FAMILY.

513
00:21:06,682 --> 00:21:09,393
OF COURSE, THAT
LITERALLY IS THE CASE

514
00:21:09,393 --> 00:21:10,937
FOR SEVERAL OF YOU.

515
00:21:13,189 --> 00:21:16,943
TONY, CARLOS, MARIE,
PLEASE, TELL YOUR FATHER

516
00:21:16,943 --> 00:21:19,820
HOW MUCH
WE'RE GOING TO MISS HIM.

517
00:21:21,155 --> 00:21:22,740
NOW, I KNOW
THAT MONICA

518
00:21:22,740 --> 00:21:25,201
HAS A LOT OF GREAT IDEAS
FOR THIS PLACE--

519
00:21:25,201 --> 00:21:28,204
WELL, YOU ALL
READ THE REVIEW--

520
00:21:28,204 --> 00:21:31,373
SO, WITHOUT MUCH
FURTHER ADO,

521
00:21:31,373 --> 00:21:35,461
I PRESENT TO YOU
OUR NEW HEAD CHEF.

522
00:21:41,508 --> 00:21:45,972
UM, I JUST WANT TO SAY, UH,
THAT WITH A PINCH OF EXCITEMENT

523
00:21:45,972 --> 00:21:49,850
A DASH OF HARD WORK
AND A DOLLOP OF COOPERATION

524
00:21:49,850 --> 00:21:52,019
WE CAN HAVE THE RECIPE...

525
00:21:56,398 --> 00:21:57,775
ARE YOU GOING TO KILL ME?

